  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A semantic web infrastructural stack for integrated science",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"A semantic web infrastructural stack for integrated science\"** This is the user's description of the system, not an invented visual metaphor. The desired language emphasizes scientific publishing and editorial clarity. Component character should be approachable and softly framed, with restrained depth and flat task panels taking priority.\n\n**Authority boundary:** the user explicitly stated that the current style is not a choice they want. This document inventories the existing implementation; it does not approve its palette, serif headings, gradients, or component styling as the future identity. The frontmatter gives exact baseline values for reproducing current behavior. Future redesign work must establish a new visual direction rather than treat these recorded values as user-mandated aesthetics. Quasar is the user-confirmed preferred UI stack; framework preference is independent of visual preference.\n\nThere are three related but distinct implementations: the shared service dashboard, the themeable k.Actors application renderer, and the comparatively primitive review interfaces. Typography and colors differ between their entry points. Their differences are evidence to preserve when diagnosing the present UI, not a deliberate global design theory.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dashboard: pale background, green accents, serif headings, rounded cards, compact telemetry labels.",
      "k.Actors: scoped light/dark variables, Quasar controls, bordered application regions.",
      "Review: native form controls, explicit fieldsets, source-oriented editors, side-by-side candidate and feedback areas.",
      "Confirmed direction: scientific editorial clarity, functional color naming, restrained depth, approachable framing."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Scope Rule",
        "body": "Application themes stay scoped to the renderer; dashboard brand values do not replace --ui-* variables.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "Authority boundary",
        "body": "Quasar is preferred. Existing styling is not the user's chosen future design direction.",
        "section": "overview"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do treat Quasar as the preferred system UI stack.",
      "Do distinguish observed baseline styles from confirmed preferences and future design decisions.",
      "Do use functional color names and keep application themes scoped.",
      "Do retain visible labels, textual states, and the existing application focus/reduced-motion behavior during maintenance.",
      "Do prioritize flat task panels and restrained depth when interpreting the user's stated preferences."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't present the current colors, gradients, serif headings, or review editor styling as an approved future identity.",
      "Don't infer a downloaded font from a fallback declaration or assume an isolated fixture shares the production cascade without checking it.",
      "Don't claim the primitive review forms represent the finished review experience.",
      "Don't infer full accessibility, authentication, or production-responsive verification from these isolated captures."
    ]
  }
